                <pb facs="0832" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg818"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Field, Acting
                        Attorney-General, to Mr. Milledge, district
                        attorney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-09-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >September</hi> 1, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Milledge</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">United States Attorney, Macon, Georgia:</hi></p>
                <p>If the marshal needs troops to aid him in serving criminal process, the
                    department commander has been ordered to furnish them. If necessary, give notice
                    to the United States attorney at Mobile.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. A. FIELD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Attorney-General.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
